messages:
Priya (sales): FYI Acme demo environment started seeing 429 spikes again during long multi-turn flows. Happens ~10-15m into a session. Theyalled out "token drift" when users paste long transcripts.
Logan (sre): Do we have trace IDs or request IDs from the window? Need to see if 429s are per-route throttles or token budget enforcement.
Priya (sales): Sent two examples: rid=rid-A3f92 and rid=rid-B7c11. Route header: x-route=chat-interactive. They said some sessions were streaming and then the client retried twice.
Nina (sales-eng): Customer uses a naive retry: ```js
async function call(){
  for(let i=0;i<3;i++){
    try { return await api.generate(payload); }
    catch(e){ await sleep(300); }
  }
}
```
Nina (sales-eng): Also their UI re-sends the full convo on reconnect which spikes token accounting.
Jules (infra): quota-bot, give me account snapshot.
quota-bot: acme-inc: daily_token_budget=1500000; used_today=1436000; per_route_limit(chat-interactive)=120/s; current_1m_rate=180/s; last_update=1887654300
Logan (sre): Current_1m_rate > per_route_limit -> this is per-route throttling causing 429s. Also high daily usage nearing 96% of budget.
Priya (sales): Customer asking for a short-term lift to get through a partner demo at 11:30 PT. They need ~400/s bursts for ~20m.
Jules (infra): We can temporary bump route cap but need to guard by token burn cutoff and auto-revert. Proposal: route cap -> 400/s for 1h, auto-revert OR if used_today > 0.98*daily_budget. Also add soft-queueing to reject excess instead of hard 429s?
Logan (sre): Soft-queueing helps but still will consume tokens if they keep resending full convo. Recommend we also enable prefix-KV caching on their session ids to reduce token use on replays.
Nina (sales-eng): Can we ask the customer to do three items: 1) implement exponential backoff + full jitter for retries, 2) stop re-sending full convo on reconnect (send delta), 3) enable streaming keepalive shorter TTL.
Priya (sales): I'm coordinating. Meanwhile, can we do the bump? Ben, need approval for temporary quota adjustment.
Ben (acct exec): Approve 1h bump to 400/s with automatic revert and alert to ops if usage > 98%. Add note: reason=partner-demo at 11:30 PT; contact=acme-demo@acme.com.
Jules (infra): Executing admin command (canary):
```
admin tools set-route-cap --account acme-inc --route chat-interactive --cap 400 --ttl 1h --revert-on-usage 0.98 --note "partner-demo"
```
quota-bot: Action started: set-route-cap acme-inc chat-interactive -> 400/s TTL 1h (initiated by Jules). ETA 35s
Logan (sre): Keeping dashboard on the account. If token burn continues to climb and hits revert threshold we'll notify. Also creating a short runbook for the customer: include sample backoff snippet and delta-send pattern.
Priya (sales): Sent the runbook link and asked them to pause any non-demo background jobs for 30m. Customer replied: "Thanks, will patch retries and pause syncs."
Nina (sales-eng): Suggested retry snippet to customer: ```js
// exponential backoff with full jitter
const retry = async (fn, attempts=5)=>{
  for(let i=0;i<attempts;i++){
    try{return await fn();}catch(e){
      const wait = Math.random() * Math.min(1000 * 2**i, 10000);
      await sleep(wait);
    }
  }
}
```
Logan (sre): After bump, monitored metrics: 429 rate fell by 85% in the next 5m. However token usage still high. We'll keep the bump but prepare to revert if they exhaust >98% budget.
Priya (sales): I'll follow up with customer post-demo and request they adopt delta updates + caching. Thanks team. :pray:
